---
description: Store and exchange dates in Gregorian; show and pick them in Shamsi
alwaysApply: true
---

# Dates

User-facing dates and times are Shamsi on screen only. The database and every send/receive path use Gregorian.

- Store a date as text `YYYY-MM-DD`, for example `2026-10-07`.
- Store a datetime as text `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS`, for example `2026-10-07T16:30:00`.
- Keep the civil clock time. Do not shift it to UTC. `schema_migrations.applied_at` is the exception: it is an internal UTC timestamp.
- Never write a Shamsi string into the database or onto an external API.
- Display with `format_shamsi_date` / `format_shamsi_datetime` from `Atten.Core`.
- When a Shamsi value is chosen or typed, convert it with `parse_shamsi_date` / `parse_shamsi_datetime` before insert or update, then store the Gregorian text.
- Do not convert calendars inside SQL. A date widget must call Core; it must not implement month tables or Shamsi math itself. Engine date functions stay in the connection layer.
